Original commit body from 3803037f2a37c8e0759df20233ad706f09479f17:

api.github.com answers /actions/jobs/<id>/logs and /actions/artifacts/<id>/zip
with a redirect to one of GitHub's numbered Azure storage accounts
(productionresultssa0, sa1, ...). ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md did not list them, so
`ci-debug --actions logs|artifact` refused by design (exit 3, host named).

Owner decision 2026-10-17 (WI-pubur discussion): list the family as
`productionresultssa*.blob.core.windows.net`, not blob.core.windows.net at
large. The ci-debug matcher now honours `*` in an entry as exactly one DNS
label and treats such an entry as a whole-host match, never a parent domain:
productionresultssa19. matches, evil.productionresultssa0. does not, and
blob.core.windows.net itself does not. The allowlist entry carries the
rationale and the scope limit (read-only GET of the signed URL only).

Verified live after the change: `logs --actions 39068691320 io-manifest`
returns the 55 KB job log; `artifact --actions 39068691320 io-manifest <dir>`
extracts 26 files, byte-identical to the copy fetched with gh under the
earlier one-off waiver. Tests: the refusal cases move to a host that stays
unlisted, the storage host gains a positive case, and the matcher test pins
the one-label rule.

Governance file (ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md); owner approval recorded on WI-pubur.

